1
00:00:01,289 --> 00:00:04,530
When there is an issue across multiple projects and you

2
00:00:04,530 --> 00:00:09,050
try to diagnose using a scattered log, this could be cumbersome.

3
00:00:09,170 --> 00:00:13,600
That's where the solution is having to have centralized logging.

4
00:00:13,840 --> 00:00:15,250
Let's see how we can do that.

5
00:00:15,329 --> 00:00:18,229
Let's say I have a project hpc2,

6
00:00:18,450 --> 00:00:22,379
and I want the log from a different project also flow

7
00:00:22,379 --> 00:00:24,719
into this specific project only.

8
00:00:24,850 --> 00:00:27,860
So let's say I go down to the log storage,

9
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:31,329
and let's create a new log bucket, central‑logs.

10
00:00:31,489 --> 00:00:34,689
Select the region and say Next and say Create bucket.

11
00:00:34,930 --> 00:00:36,909
Now let me go to the other project.

12
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:40,620
In this hpc3 project, let me go down to the logs.

13
00:00:40,620 --> 00:00:44,130
Here under the Logging, I'm going to select the Log router.

14
00:00:44,369 --> 00:00:47,819
In the Log router on the top, click on Create sink,

15
00:00:47,889 --> 00:00:51,470
give the sink name, say Next, select the sink service.

16
00:00:51,689 --> 00:00:53,529
I'm going to select the service as Logging bucket.

17
00:00:53,900 --> 00:01:00,340
And I have to choose a log bucket which I have created into our hpc project 2.

18
00:01:00,459 --> 00:01:04,000
So I will say Use a log bucket in another project.

19
00:01:04,099 --> 00:01:05,699
Now in the Sink destination,

20
00:01:05,940 --> 00:01:10,379
let's copy the path of our bucket which we have created in the

21
00:01:10,379 --> 00:01:14,160
project 2 and say Next. In the inclusion filter, leave it empty

22
00:01:14,260 --> 00:01:16,169
so that it will include all the logs.

23
00:01:16,379 --> 00:01:21,410
Say Next and say Create sink. Now our sink has been successfully created.

24
00:01:21,470 --> 00:01:24,389
Now we need to do one more thing because this sink has to

25
00:01:24,389 --> 00:01:28,529
write the data into our project to log bucket, so we need

26
00:01:28,529 --> 00:01:30,470
to provide the IAM access.

27
00:01:30,669 --> 00:01:34,269
So what I'm going to do is, so in our log sink which we have created,

28
00:01:34,379 --> 00:01:36,910
click on three dots, see View sink details,

29
00:01:37,019 --> 00:01:38,989
and there you see Writer identity.

30
00:01:39,110 --> 00:01:44,150
So copy this writer identity and now go to the project 2 and go to the IAM.

31
00:01:44,480 --> 00:01:49,040
And here, give the log writer permission to this specific

32
00:01:49,040 --> 00:01:50,639
service account which we have copied.

33
00:01:50,839 --> 00:01:52,760
So say Grant access, copy the name,

34
00:01:52,910 --> 00:01:57,169
and under the role, select the role as Logs Bucket Writer and say Save.

35
00:01:57,430 --> 00:02:02,980
Now the project 3 will be able to copy all the logs from there to the project 2,

36
00:02:03,120 --> 00:02:05,800
and in the project 2 we could have the centralized log.

37
00:02:05,959 --> 00:02:09,479
Similarly, we can do the same thing with the other project also.

38
00:02:09,610 --> 00:02:09,929
In fact,

39
00:02:10,130 --> 00:02:14,330
you can do this thing at the organization or at the folder level so that you

40
00:02:14,330 --> 00:02:17,929
don't have to repeatedly do it at each and every project level.

41
00:02:18,210 --> 00:02:22,330
Now if you want to watch all those logs in one central location,

42
00:02:22,649 --> 00:02:25,850
let's go to the Log Explorer in the project 2.

43
00:02:26,050 --> 00:02:29,160
And here in the Log Explorer, you can see the centrally

44
00:02:29,160 --> 00:02:31,240
log from all the different projects.

45
00:02:31,330 --> 00:02:34,850
So that's how you can set up your centralized log repository.
